# distribution/docker/.dockerignore — keep the runtime image build context lean.
#
# Phase 21 D-02 / Plan 21-03 Task 1.
#
# Build-context discipline rationale:
#   - The runtime Dockerfile only needs `tools/ChromiumPrefetch/` (for the
#     chromium-builder stage), `_output/linux-${TARGETARCH}/` (for the runtime
#     stage COPY), and `distribution/docker/root/` (for the s6-overlay scripts).
#   - Everything else is noise that bloats the buildx context upload.
#   - `_output/` is excluded as a whole, then the per-arch subtree is
#     re-included via explicit COPY in the Dockerfile (Docker treats COPY paths
#     against the build context, so the file must be present even when
#     .dockerignore excludes its parent — buildx does this correctly).
#
# Note: this .dockerignore is used when `docker buildx build` is invoked with
# `--file distribution/docker/Dockerfile --context .` (repo root context).
# .dockerignore is resolved relative to the build context root, NOT the
# Dockerfile location — so this file must be a copy/symlink/mirror at repo
# root as well, OR the CI step must reference this path explicitly via
# `DOCKER_BUILDX_DOCKERIGNORE_PATH` (buildx-specific). Plan 21-04 wires the
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml docker_publish job; it documents the path
# resolution there.

# ─── VCS ───
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.gitkeep
.github/

# ─── Planning + docs (massive, never needed at build time) ───
.planning/
docs/
*.md
!distribution/docker/**/*.md
DIVERGENCE.md
README.md
PROJECT_CONTEXT.md
CLAUDE.md
**/CLAUDE.md

# ─── Test output + dev artifacts ───
_tests/
.playwright-mcp/
TestResult.xml
TestResult.html
**/*.trx

# ─── Node / frontend dev ───
frontend/node_modules/
**/node_modules/
yarn-error.log
npm-debug.log

# ─── .NET dev artifacts ───
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/*.user
**/*.suo
**/.vs/
**/AppPackages/
**/BundleArtifacts/

# ─── Editor / IDE ───
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ─── Docker self-exclusion (avoid pulling our own build context in) ───
distribution/docker-build/_output/
distribution/docker-build/_artifacts/

# ─── Output that is NOT the per-arch published artifacts ───
# _output/ wholesale-excluded; the Dockerfile COPYs _output/linux-${TARGETARCH}/
# explicitly, which buildx honors as an exception to this ignore.
_output/
!_output/linux-amd64/
!_output/linux-arm64/

# ─── Misc transient ───
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
*.cbz.tmp
.playwright-report/
playwright-report/
